# /fix — Bug Fix Path

Use this path for fixing bugs, errors, and broken behavior.

## Usage

```
/fix                    — general bug fix (prompts for area)
/fix css                — CSS layout or styling bug
/fix auth               — authentication or authorization bug
/fix data               — data service, MongoDB, or API data bug
/fix ui                 — UI component or interaction bug
/fix api                — backend route, server, or integration bug
/fix other              — anything that doesn't fit the above
```

## Loads by area

| Area | Standards loaded |
|------|-----------------|
| `css` | `docs/agent/standards-angular.md` (UI, CSS & Folder Structure section) + `cssLayer` skill |
| `auth` | `docs/agent/standards-security.md` + `auth-and-logging` skill (covers crypto) |
| `data` | `docs/agent/standards-domain.md` + `docs/agent/standards-backend.md` |
| `ui` | `docs/agent/standards-angular.md` (Angular 19 & Reactivity section) + `docs/agent/standards-domain.md` |
| `api` | `docs/agent/standards-backend.md` + `docs/agent/standards-security.md` |
| `other` | `docs/agent/` (path-scoped) + `CLAUDE.md` |

## Invokes

- `investigate` — root cause analysis before any fix is applied
- After a working fix exists, refine it to production quality against `docs/agent/standards-angular.md` (naming, shared pure helpers instead of one-off copies, no nested async chains, units under 300 lines)

## Typical flow

1. User describes the bug (area + symptom).
2. `investigate` traces the root cause (checks recent changes, failure history, source).
3. Fix is implemented atomically — one targeted change.
4. Review the fix for code quality, edge cases, and consistency against `docs/agent/standards-angular.md`; a stylesheet touched → `cssLayer`.
5. `npm run build` / `npm run lint` pass. Human commits via `git-agent` prep.

## Hard rules

- NEVER fix a symptom without identifying the root cause first.
- `npm run build` must pass before committing.
- Match the file's existing style; never reformat untouched lines.
- No semicolons in any `.ts` file touched during the fix.
- 3-strike rule: at most 3 autonomous fix attempts in scoped files; then STOP and report.
- A fix that needs its own checkout (this folder is on `main` or busy): `node scripts/worktree-clean.mjs add fix-<NNN> --branch fix/<slug>`, and when the fix is merged, `node scripts/worktree-clean.mjs remove <folder>`. Never delete a folder any other way; a folder it keeps prints why.
